ticut is an AA/EEO Employer. (HR25-52) Temporary University Specialist (Program Coordinator) – UConn Hartford – Posted December 17, 2025 Temporary University Specialist (Program Coordinator) UConn Hartford; Micro-Internship Program INTRODUCTION The Program Coordinator will support a cohort of undergraduate first-generation students at the Hartford Campus and an employer network requiring strong organizational, communication, and program management skills. The ideal candidate will ensure the high-quality administration of the program by supporting students, coordinating employer partners, managing application systems, collaborating with campus partners (RISE, CAPS, others as needed), and facilitating professional development. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Program Administration & Communications Manage onboarding, documentation, and communication for 15–20 interns and 15 – 20 employer supervisors. Manage workflow and relationship management through a CRM (12Twenty) to ensure all opportunities are published, applications are screened, and shared with internship sites Develop and maintain scalable systems for tracking hours, attendance, and deliverables. Employer Engagement Build and maintain relationships with a larger network of community-based internship hosts. Ensure consistent quality in project descriptions and supervisor expectations across all placements. Provide ongoing support to employers throughout the cycle. Student Preparation & Support Host expanded resume, application, and interview preparation workshops for a larger applicant pool. Conduct weekly check-ins with each intern (15–20 students), documenting progress and addressing issues. Create scalable guidance tools (FAQs, templates, resource sheets). Professional Development Course Co-facilitate larger PD Friday sessions with RISE/CAPS Create materials designed for larger cohort engagement. Support interns in preparing for final presentations. Evaluation & Reporting Track participation, hours, employer satisfaction, and student learning outcomes across 15–20 placements. Prepare a comprehensive program evaluation highlighting key metrics, themes, and recommendations. Support donor stewardship with data summaries and program impact visuals. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree. Demonstrated written communication skills. Proven organizational skills and attention to detail. Experience using Microsoft Office 365 (Teams, Outlook, Excel, OneDrive) and demonstrated ability to learn new career development platforms. Experience working with diverse and first-generation student populations. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities and maintain timely follow-through. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience in career services, student affairs, community engagement, or workforce development. Experience designing or facilitating workshops or training. Familiarity with UConn systems such as 12Twenty, HuskyCT, KFS, or Handshake. Experience partnering with nonprofits or local community organizations. APPOINTMENT TERMS The position is on location at the Hartford Campus, University of Connecticut Hours: 8 – 10 hours/week for 20 weeks Expected Pay: $27.50 Start Date: February 23, 2026 – June 26, 2026 TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate will be contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please send a cover letter , resume, and list of three professional references with contact information to wiley.dawson@uconn.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce.  The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner.  This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all.  We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same.  All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO Employer. (HR25-51) Temporary University Specialist – The Department of Student Activities, Storrs Campus – Posted September 26, 2025 Temporary University Specialist The Department of Student Activities, Storrs Campus JOB SUMMARY The Department of Student Activities (DSA) seeks applicants for a Special Payroll Marketing position for a duration of 6 months. This position is critical in advancing two institutional and departmental priorities: Ensuring compliance with ADA web accessibility standards Establishing a sustainable alumni communications and engagement infrastructure This position will work closely with areas/offices and a Graduate Assistant (GA) within DSA to plan, develop, and execute strategic marketing initiatives, internal and external communications, and compliance driving digital accessibility projects. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES ADA & Digital Compliance: Audit, update, and transition DSA websites into the University’s new Cynder theme. Ensure all digital content (websites, social media, promotional materials, newsletters) meets ADA Title II accessibility standards. Serve as departmental liaison to University Communications and IT for accessibility and branding compliance. Marketing and Communications: Plan and develop marketing strategies designed to attract target audiences and other potential users of departmental programs, events, and services. Design and distribute print, electronic, and video material to promote all areas within Student Activities, employing content design, development, photo editing, script development, etc. Design and manage the use of all marketing and branding materials for DSA programs, serving as a liaison with Office of Branding and Licensure. Create and develop a monthly department newsletter, ensuring regular and engaging content to be distributed across campuses. Alumni Engagement: Build foundational alumni communications systems Develop branded content and storytelling strategies aligned with institutional advancement Support alumni database development and engagement initiatives to create lasing connections with graduates. Events and Campaigns: Co-Manage, schedule, and create regularly posted content for social media accounts (e.g., Instagram, Facebook). Manage, curate, and ensure the collection of up-to-date photo documentation of programs, events, and activities. General duties: Serve as a resource to department staff regarding effective promotional strategies and problem-solving. Stay informed about available media products, services, and costs to maximize promotional efforts. Perform duties as assigned specific to programmatic and/or department wide needs. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree in marketing, communications, graphic design, advertising, or a related field with at least two years of relevant experience in marketing, promotions, or communications, ideally in a higher education or student affairs setting. Demonstrated experience in social media management and content creation. Experience managing websites and using content management systems (CMS) like WordPress / Aurora. Experience in graphic design and proficiency with software such as Adobe Creative Suite (Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign) and Canva. Strong writing and communication skills, with experience in creating engaging content for various channels, including newsletters, websites, and social media. Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously, work collaboratively with team members, and meet deadlines. Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to work effectively with diverse groups and stakeholders, including students, staff, and external partners. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Knowledge of/experience marketing, advertising, promoting events and activities, preferably on college campus. Demonstrated ability to design and distribute both print and digital materials, including newsletters, brochures, and promotional videos. 3 years of experience working in a higher education environment or with student programs. Experience coordinating large-scale events and understanding the marketing needs of university-level activities. Knowledge of digital marketing trends, SEO (search engine optimization), email marketing, and video content creation Familiarity with university branding guidelines and working with licensing offices. Flexibility and adaptability to manage the dynamic nature of the role and the evolving needs of the department. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a temporary 6-month position, with an hourly rate of $25.00 per hour. The role requires a commitment of 30 hours per week with the potential for a hybrid schedule following an initial onboarding period on campus; subject to departmental needs and supervisor approval. TO APPLY Please submit cover letter, resume and contact information for three professional references to Diane Busey at diane.busey@uconn.edu Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce.  The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner.  This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all.  We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same.  All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO Employer [HR25-43] Public Service Technician (Program Assistant) – UConn Extension- Farmington, CT – Posted August 26, 2025 Public Service Technician (Program Assistant) UConn Extension- Farmington, CT The Department of Extension at the University of Connecticut is seeking a temporary program assistant (40 hours a week) to deliver and coordinate 4-H educational programs primarily in Hartford County. This position is funded by the Advancing 4-H Careers in Food and Agriculture via Biotechnology and STEM (FANE) grant program. The program is funded through the National Institute of Food and Agriculture (NIFA) / United States Department of Agriculture (USDA) and provides research based, quality 4-H educational programming to youth in grades 9-12. The successful candidate will work under the direction of the Project Team and report to the 4-H Extension Educator. Activities will occur at various community sites in the Greater Hartford area and various field trip locations. In addition to planning and delivering instruction in biotechnology topics, the successful applicant will maintain program records, create program promotional documents, engage with community organizations, create educational outreach content, chaperone youth field trips and other program related tasks at the Hartford County Extension Center in Farmington, Connecticut. Instructional hours will occur in the afternoon/evenings with some weekends. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Delivering educational content on STEM and biotechnology to youth. Engage 4-H participants in game development related to STEM and Biotechnology related content. Support teen 4-H members in the development of outreach materials that communicate to their peers and adults how biotechnology, agriculture and careers. Create agriculture, biotechnology and career educational content. Collect data through pre-and post-tests and compile results. Organize and maintain supplies and records from 4-H activities. Assist with outreach or promotional activities. Plan and chaperone 4-H field trips, including driving and transporting 4-H participants in rental vehicles or traveling between sites. Independently implement programing. Perform related duties as required. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Associates degree or equivalent educational experience. Demonstrated experience of one or more years delivering programming to youth in an informal or formal setting. Familiarity with STEM or related concepts. Demonstrated organizational, time management, and communication skills. Previous experience utilizing computer skills, including Microsoft Suite. Demonstrated experience managing groups of youth. Ability to lift program materials and set up meeting spaces for programming. Previous experience working as part of a team. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience in working with audiences of various backgrounds. Experience using educational technology for instruction. Interest in working with teenage youth. Familiarity with 4-H programming. Experience using social media for professional purposes. Bachelor’s or master’s degree. APPOINTMENT TERMS The successful incumbent must possess and retain a valid driver’s license. The anticipated start date of this position is September 2025. The appointment term is six months with the possibility of continuation up to an additional six months dependent upon program needs, funding availability, and performance. Compensation will be $25 per hour, for 40 hours per week. The selected incumbent will be required to maintain the agreed upon work hours/schedule, which may include nights and weekends. The incumbent must have a valid driver’s license and availability to work on nights and weekends. TO APPLY Please submit a cover letter , resume and names of three professional references with email and phone numbers to jennifer.cushman@uconn.edu . Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University Community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO Employer. HR25-37 Research Technician [FRAME Lab Coordinator] – University of Connecticut, Stamford Campus – Posted June 3, 2025 Research Technician [FRAME Lab Coordinator] University of Connecticut, Stamford Campus The UConn Stamford Family Resilience And Mindfulness Empowerment (FRAME) Lab, directed by Dr. Na Zhang in the Department of Human Development and Family Sciences, is looking for a research coordinator beginning as soon as possible. The FRAME Lab Coordinator will work closely with Dr. Na Zhang and oversee research-related projects, tasks and activities at the UConn Stamford campus. This is a hybrid position and involves some in-person tasks. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES The responsibilities of the FRAME Lab Coordinator will include: Managing research tasks that include human subjects’ recruitment, screening, eligibility determination, scheduling of data collection (in the lab or virtual). Testing online surveys and administering structured interviews. Managing and maintaining databases, IRB protocols. Updating lab news on lab websites. Attending weekly meetings. Assisting with conference abstracts and manuscripts submissions. Other miscellaneous tasks as needed. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS A Bachelor’s degree in Human Development and Family Sciences, Psychology, Sociology, Social Work, or related fields Strong interpersonal communication skills Strong computer skills using Microsoft Office software (Outlook, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, OneDrive) Strong project management skills (including tracking progress and deadlines, taking meeting notes, preparing meeting agenda) Excellent ability to work independently Detail-oriented and excellent at administrative tasks PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience working in a research lab that involves families or youth Experience administering studies in Qualtrics and/or Redcap. Clinical research experience (e.g., randomized controlled trials) CITI training certificate (Collaborative Institutional Training Initiative APPOINTMENT TERMS This position is part-time. The initial appointment would be 20 hours per week for six months, with the possibility to extend. Start date is negotiable. This is a hybrid position that requires working in the lab at UConn Stamford building located at 1 University Place, Stamford, CT 06901. Salary: $17-$20/hour depending on experience, 20 hours/week TO APPLY Please email a resume/curriculum vitae , a cover letter of interests and experience, and the names of 3 references to Dr. Na Zhang ( nazhang@uconn.edu ). Applications will be received on a rolling basis until the position is filled. Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . The University of Connecticut is committed to building and supporting a multicultural and diverse community of students, faculty and staff. The diversity of students, faculty and staff continues to increase, as does the number of honors students, valedictorians and salutatorians who consistently make UConn their top choice. More than 100 research centers and institutes serve the University’s teaching, research, diversity and outreach missions, leading to UConn’s ranking as one of the nation’s top research universities. UConn’s faculty and staff are the critical link to fostering and expanding our vibrant, multicultural and diverse University community. As an Affirmative Action/Equal Employment Opportunity employer, UConn encourages applications from women, veterans, people with disabilities and members of traditionally underrepresented populations. HR25-26 Temporary University Specialist – Admissions Department, Stamford Campus – Posted April 21, 2025 Temporary University Specialist Admissions Department, Stamford Campus The UConn Stamford Admissions Office is seeking a Temporary University Specialist to support administrative functions. Reporting to the Admissions Officer, this position is based at the Stamford Campus and will require evening and weekend hours. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Manage front office operations, including visitor interactions, appointment scheduling, answering phones, and admissions inquiries. Coordinate the master calendar to ensure proper scheduling and coverage. Organize and oversee high school and community-based organization visits, including outreach, agenda planning, and day-of logistics. Confirm scheduled tours, follow up with no-shows, and gather feedback from visitors. Update presentation materials regularly to meet the needs of various student populations and visit programs. Support major campus events such as Open Houses, UConn Bound Days, Student Panels, Shadow Day Programs, Specialty Major Programs and more. Serve on the Application Review Committee and analyze prospective student applications. Act as a knowledgeable resource for campus visitors, including prospective students and the general public. Represent UConn Stamford and the Admissions Department at local community events Provide campus and Residence Hall tours to students and guests. Utilize a Customer Relations Management System to check and confirm students’ application statuses, track missing materials, and record interactions. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree with one year of experience. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to work effectively with others. Proficiency with Microsoft Office products, especially Excel, Word, and Outlook. Willingness and the ability to work nights and weekends to support Admissions events and initiatives. Interest in working with high school and college students. Self-motivated with the ability to work autonomously. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Prior experience in a higher education setting. Demonstrated ability to plan, coordinate, and execute events. Knowledge of the admissions and recruitment cycle. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a 6-month, in-person appointment for 35-40 hours per week, with the possibility of extension. The weekly schedule will vary based on campus and community events, requiring frequent evening and weekend commitments. The hourly rate is $20 – $25, commensurate with experience. TO APPLY Interested candidates should submit a resume , a letter of application that demonstrates how you meet the qualifications and requirements of this position, and contact information for three professional references with name, title, phone number, and email. Screening will begin immediately. Applications can be sent to beahuskystamford@uconn.edu All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner.  This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all.  We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO Employer. HR25-20 Temporary University Specialist (Admin Support to Director) – Center for Clean Energy Engineering – Posted March 24, 2025 Temporary University Specialist (Admin Support to Director) Center for Clean Energy Engineering JOB SUMMARY The University of Connecticut’s Center for Clean Energy Engineering (C2E2) is seeking a dynamic and team-oriented candidate for a part-time Temporary University Specialist to support the Director for Center for Clean Energy Engineering. As a crucial member of the Center’s administrative team, the ideal candidate will demonstrate attention to detail, organizational skills, and self-motivation. JOB RESPONSIBILITIES Provide administrative and program support to the Center Director. Manage the Director’s calendar by scheduling appointments, coordinating meetings, and arranging travel logistics, including processing expenses through the Concur system. Coordinate the Director’s signatory commitments. Organize and schedule meetings with faculty, staff, and external partners to support research development and faculty initiatives, preparing agendas and managing follow-up actions. Compile, organize, and track documents and data from multiple sources for research proposals, project reports, and presentations as requested by the Director. Act as a primary resource for information and procedures related to the Center’s administrative processes, offering support and guidance to internal and external stakeholders. Assist in drafting, editing, and formatting communications, presentations, and reports. Support project management by keeping track of deadlines, following up on action items, and ensuring tasks are completed on time. Perform additional administrative duties as assigned. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree and two years of related experience OR an equivalent combination of education and experience. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple high-priority tasks and projects with competing deadlines in a busy environment. Demonstrated experience providing organizational support in a team environment. Proficient in the use of all MS Office applications, especially Outlook and managing calendars. Demonstrated excellence in attention to detail, written communication, organization, interpersonal skills. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience in higher education and sponsored research. Experience working in a fast-paced, complex, multi-faceted office environment. Ability to expertly manage time and deadlines, and juggle multiple competing priorities. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a part time, temporary position of 15 to 20 hours per week with an expected duration of 6 months with the possibility for extension, located on the Storrs campus. Salary will be commensurate with the candidate’s background and experience. TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY To apply, please send a cover letter, resume and the names and contact details of three professional references to Hillary MacLachlan at hillary.maclachlan@uconn.edu . Screening of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce.  The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner.  This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all.  We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same.  All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO Employer. HR25-14 Temporary University Specialist – School of Social Work – Posted February 3, 2025 Temporary University Specialist School of Social Work The University of Connecticut School of Social Work is seeking applicants for a temporary position as a Temporary University Specialist in the Dean’s Office. Under the direction of the Dean and Associate Dean of Academic Affairs, this position assists in managing several high-level administrative functions in the School of Social Work Dean’s Office. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Responsible for scheduling meetings and managing calendars for the Dean and Associate Dean for Academic Affairs. Performs office management duties; directs the workflow and supervises the processing of administrative and personnel paperwork; reviews paperwork for accuracy and adherence to the School of Social Work and University of Connecticut policies and procedures. Responsible for special short-term projects that require planning, coordination, and Responsible for administrative support for Faculty Search Committees, including liaison with Human Resources, electronic record keeping, correspondence and coordination of candidate campus visits as needed. Responsible for administrative supports related to faculty Promotion, Tenure, and Review as needed. Handles confidential records in a professional manner. Performs related duties as required. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS 1-2 years of related experience. Demonstrated ability to provide administrative and program support. Demonstrated ability to work independently and regularly exercise judgment regarding a wide variety of administrative and student matters. Good interpersonal and organizational skills. Proficient writing and communication skills. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite, including Outlook, Excel, etc. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience with managing schedules. Work experience in a college or university academic setting. Familiarity with University of Connecticut/State of Connecticut regulations, policies, and procedures. Familiarity with UConn systems, such as Interfolio, Student Administration, and PageUp. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a temporary, 20-35 hours per week position. The appointment will begin as soon as possible and last through the end of July 2025. This position is based on the Hartford Campus, with a hybrid (both in-person and remote) work schedule. The salary is $25/hour. TO APPLY Please submit a letter of application , resume , and the names and contact information of three professional references to sswsearch@uconn.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. (Ref HR25-5) Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce.  The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner.  This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all.  We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same.  All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO Employer. (HR25-5) 2024 Research Technician, Center for Environmental Sciences and Engineering – Posted November 21, 2024 Research Technician Center for Environmental Sciences and Engineering JOB SUMMARY The University of Connecticut is pleased to invite applications for a Research Technician position in the Center for Environmental Sciences and Engineering. The successful candidate will contribute to the management of research projects on salt marsh restoration and biogeochemistry as part of Dr. Ashley Helton’s biogeochemistry lab group. The position offers a unique opportunity to collaborate as part of a large, interdisciplinary research team focused on coastal ecosystem dynamics. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBLIITIES Assist in the design, implementation, and management of laboratory and field experiments in salt marsh ecosystems Maintain and operate laboratory equipment for analysis of water, soil, or gases Lead collection and processing of soil, water, and greenhouse gas samples Follow and develop standard protocols for field and laboratory procedures and QAQC of laboratory data Coordinate, train, and work with undergraduate research assistants Organize and manage large empirical datasets MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s Degree in Natural Resources, Ecology, Environmental Science, or related field Experience conducting field research Experience operating analytical equipment for analysis of water, soil, or gases Strong, independent work ethic and time management skills Excellent interpersonal and communication skills Detail oriented PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Master’s Degree in Natural Resources, Ecology, Environmental Science, or related field Experience conducting field research in wetland or coastal ecosystems Experience maintaining and troubleshooting analytical equipment for analysis of water, soil, or gases Training and experience in data management and analysis APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a temporary, full-time position based in Storrs.  Annual salary is $50,000 to $55,000, commensurate with experience. The start date for this position is negotiable but preferred in January 2025.  The position begins with a 6-month appointment with the possibility of renewal for up to two years, depending upon funding and job performance. TO APPLY To apply, please email a cover letter , resume or CV , and contact information for three references to Ashley.helton@uconn.edu .  Please include – “Research Technician Application” as the subject line. Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment background check, if required. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce.  The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner.  This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all.  We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same.  All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO Employer. [HR24-113] Temporary University Specialist – Student Health and Wellness, Stamford Campus – Posted November 5, 2024 Temporary University Specialist [ Mental Health Clinician] Student Health and Wellness, Stamford Campus JOB SUMMARY Student Health and Wellness (SHaW) Mental Health at the University of Connecticut is searching for a licensed clinician to serve as the Clinical Case Manager to provide direct clinical case management services, including assessment and brief psychotherapy, emergency care, psycho-educational services, and consulting services to the University community. This is a temporary position, 35 hours per week for up to 12 weeks. SHaW is committed to diversity and inclusion, competence in working with culturally and ethnically diverse populations, and awareness of how issues of difference, power, and privilege manifest in higher education environments. The ideal candidate promotes health equity and reduces health disparities by demonstrating and supporting an understanding, sensitivity, and appreciation for health equity, social justice, cultural humility, and inclusiveness. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Provides psychotherapeutic counseling to individuals, couples, and groups, consulting with other professionals as necessary; diagnoses, assesses, and treats emotional and functional disorders through brief model psychotherapy. Provides emergency on-call service and crisis intervention for students who have psychiatric emergencies. Prepares required clinical records and case reports in a timely manner and carries on necessary correspondence. Performs clinical assessment, brief intervention, referral, and follow-up to students presenting with a wide range of mental health needs. May train and supervise other health professionals, field placement students/trainees, and volunteers. Conducts workshops and outreach services designed to provide mental health education to students, staff, faculty, administrators, and parents. May prepare narrative and statistical reports of activities for use in the evaluation of the mental health program. May compile data to analyze and identify risks, trends, and gaps in the program. Communicates and consults with appropriate university administrators, stakeholders, and various mental health and academic faculty. Make referrals to and consult with other mental health agencies offering specialized care beyond the scope of Student Health and Wellness Mental Health Services. May seek funding for and conduct studies on mental health issues; may publish or present findings in appropriate professional journals or forums/conferences. Serves as a resource and consultant to the University community on matters relating to the well-being of students within the limits of confidentiality. Assists with developing and maintaining policies and procedures to govern the counseling center. Ensures adherence to best practices. Serves on departmental and/or University committees representing Student Health and Wellness and applicable policies and procedures to stakeholders and constituencies. Performs related work as required. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Master’s or Doctoral degree in psychology, social work, counseling, marriage and family therapy, or a related field. Must possess or must obtain Connecticut Psychologist, Clinical Social Worker, or related licensure within one year of hire. One year of related experience, which may include hours for obtaining the license. Must have a demonstrated understanding of and stated commitment to diversity, inclusion, and equity issues in the delivery of clinical services. Demonstrated experience working with diverse populations. Previous experience working effectively and collegially as part of an interdisciplinary behavioral health care team. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS State of CT Licensed Psychologist (Ph.D or Psy.D), Clinical Social Worker (LCSW), Licensed Professional Counselor (LPC), or Licensed Alcohol and Drug Counselor (LADC). Demonstrated experience providing culturally responsive mental health services to college students. Demonstrated training in brief treatment models. Demonstrated expertise in a minimum of one specific treatment relevant to collegiate mental health (for example eating disorders, attention deficit disorder). Demonstrated experience working with a minimum of one specific population in college settings (for example LGBTQ, non-traditional students, students of color, etc.). APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a temporary position, up to 35 hours per week for up to 12 weeks. The hourly rate is up to $55 per hour, commensurate with experience. This position is based at the Stamford Campus and reports to the Director of Clinical Case Management. TO APPLY Interested candidates should submit a resume , a cover letter that demonstrates how they meet the qualifications and requirements of this position, and contact information for three professional references with Name, Title, Phone, and Email. Applications can be sent to laurie.loehr@uconn.edu . Screening will begin immediately. Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce.  The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner.  This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all.  We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same.  All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO Employer. [HR24-109] Educational Program Coordinator (Temporary University Specialist) – Department of Nutritional Sciences – Posted October 7, 2024 Educational Program Coordinator (Temporary University Specialist) Online Programs Assistant Department of Nutritional Sciences – Storrs (50%) JOB SUMMARY The Department of Nutritional Sciences, a part of the College of Agriculture, Health and Natural Resources, at the University of Connecticut, seeks applicants for a part-time (50%) Online Programs Coordinator. The Online Programs Coordinator will provide administrative and programmatic support to the Department of Nutritional Science’s expanding online programs. The Online Programs Coordinator will report to the Director of Online Programs and will be based out of the Storrs Campus. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Serves as a resource to current and prospective students, staff, faculty and the public regarding Nutritional Sciences online programing. Coordinates program logistics for students, faculty, and staff by arranging and securing facilities, virtual and in-person logistics, schedules, catering arrangements, post event surveys, and related items. Plans and executes several aspects of program events and student outreach, recruitment, onboarding, and advising activities. Handles routine and specialized inquiries via telephone, email, or in-person and directs them to the appropriate contact as appropriate. Assists students with academic advising, record changes, processes necessary academic forms, and maintains accurate academic records. Explains program policies, procedures, and requirements. Assembles data and prepares statistical, summary, and/or historical reports as needed. Develops, maintains, and updates a collection of resource materials, program information, and promotional materials for student recruitment, advising, career/professional development, and general Nutritional Sciences Department information; assists in updating materials as needed. Updates website, student resources and communications, and outgoing recruitment materials as needed. Prepares, organizes, and proofs documents for various program and administrative meetings. Reviews, copies, edits, and/or develops research, informational, and promotional materials for the program. Assists in the preparation and tracking of program budgets, and monitors expenditures for events and program activities, as assigned. Assists other departmental staff with administrative tasks. Performs related work as required. POSITION EXPECTATIONS Must be willing to work some weekend or evening hours MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Master’s Degree in Nutrition or a related field with two to three years of clinical experience. RDN or equivalent credential. Excellent interpersonal skills with the ability to effectively communicate verbally and in writing, complemented by strong customer service skills. Excellent organizational skills, with attention to detail. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with individuals of diverse cultural, social, and educational backgrounds. Proficient in the Microsoft Office suite (Word, Excel, Outlook, etc.) Demonstrated experience managing schedules, calendaring, and event planning. Proven ability to work independently and in a team setting while regularly exercising judgment regarding administrative details and procedures. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience in academic and outreach programs in a university or collegiate setting. Experience with Blackboard or other instructional programs. Demonstrated ability to work effectively with communication technologies, including experience with social media platforms and website maintenance. APPOINTMENT TERMS This position is 20 hours a week, and the schedule will be flexible and will be determined prior to hire between supervisor and successful candidate. The appointment term will be for six months with the possibility of extension. Once hired, specific days and times worked will be discussed with the Nutritional Sciences Department Head and Online Programs Director. The salary starts at $31.00 per hour. TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please submit a letter of application, resume, and the names and contact information of three professional references to Dr. Catherine Andersen ( catherine.andersen@uconn.edu ). Please include the subject line: “Applicant for Educational Programs Coordinator”. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce.  The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner.  This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all.  We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members 